# Line endings are mixed across the repository: some files are committed with
# CRLF, some with LF. That is invisible until a tool rewrites a file, at which
# point a twenty line change shows up as a four hundred line diff and stops
# being reviewable.
#
# From here on Git normalises text to LF in the repository and checks it out
# in whatever the platform uses.
#
# Files already committed with CRLF keep it until they are renormalised. That
# is one command — `git add --renormalize . && git commit` — deliberately left
# out of this change: it touches most files in the repository and would bury
# every other change under a whitespace commit. Worth doing on a quiet branch.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.svg text
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.pdf binary
